              "text": "dànjì is built from dàn 'thin, slack' and jì 'a season', both inherited from Middle Chinese, damX and kjwijH (Guangyun, in Baxter's transcription), which glosses the first as a thin taste and the second as the youngest of brothers; the sense 'a season' is not given there."
