          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "节假日 (jiéjiàrì) is built from 节 'a festival', 假 'leave' and 日 'a day', all inherited from Middle Chinese, tset, kaeH and nyit (Guangyun, in Baxter's transcription), which glosses the first as the joint of a bamboo stem and the second 'to borrow' and 'leave'; the sense 'a festival' for the first is not given there."
